{"uid":"ba5fbb3cd8d7b7f6","name":"test_a_cold_positive_tail_fallback_can_render_the_entire_backlog_exactly","fullName":"tests.test_hub_real_render_cap_whole_call#test_a_cold_positive_tail_fallback_can_render_the_entire_backlog_exactly","historyId":"fd3db2917a48e1a8a644ae6498b1ac90","time":{"start":1791980382218,"stop":1791980383037,"duration":819},"description":"Task cure-01-04-2 (D.1; DoD 4, criterion 3): the falsifying case the\n    review found at e5cf72a2 -- a COLD run (no `render_index.json`, no\n    legacy `collapse_index.json` either) with 1,000 non-rendering\n    `message_end` padding lines between the streamed text and the run's\n    end, asked for a small POSITIVE tail (2). The fast indexed path\n    answers `None` (nothing to walk), so the growing-bound fallback runs;\n    each round doubles the bound (2, 4, 8, 16, 32) because there is always\n    more raw history to read and the doubled request never yields 2\n    rendered lines, and once `_TAIL_GROWTH_ROUNDS_BEFORE_FULL_ASK` rounds\n    are spent it jumps straight to `_TAIL_FULL_ASK_BOUND` -- which, for\n    this fixture's raw content-line count, is the round that finally\n    reads (and, on the live surface, is asked to serve) the ENTIRE raw\n    backlog, not a bounded slice of it. Both real `ui_server.\n    rendered_log_lines` surfaces (the live API proxy and the dead-run\n    on-disk merge) still render the exact same last-2-lines tail a full,\n    uncapped render of the whole transcript would, proving the fallback's\n    correctness even when it reads everything -- and `_TAIL_FULL_ASK_BOUND`\n    itself is read from production, never a raised or re-declared literal\n    in this test.","descriptionHtml":"<p>Task cure-01-04-2 (D.1; DoD 4, criterion 3): the falsifying case the<br />\nreview found at e5cf72a2 -- a COLD run (no <code>render_index.json</code>, no<br />\nlegacy <code>collapse_index.json</code> either) with 1,000 non-rendering<br />\n<code>message_end</code> padding lines between the streamed text and the run's<br />\nend, asked for a small POSITIVE tail (2). The fast indexed path<br />\nanswers <code>None</code> (nothing to walk), so the growing-bound fallback runs;<br />\neach round doubles the bound (2, 4, 8, 16, 32) because there is always<br />\nmore raw history to read and the doubled request never yields 2<br />\nrendered lines, and once <code>_TAIL_GROWTH_ROUNDS_BEFORE_FULL_ASK</code> rounds<br />\nare spent it jumps straight to <code>_TAIL_FULL_ASK_BOUND</code> -- which, for<br />\nthis fixture's raw content-line count, is the round that finally<br />\nreads (and, on the live surface, is asked to serve) the ENTIRE raw<br />\nbacklog, not a bounded slice of it. Both real <code>ui_server. rendered_log_lines</code> surfaces (the live API proxy and the dead-run<br />\non-disk merge) still render the exact same last-2-lines tail a full,<br />\nuncapped render of the whole transcript would, proving the fallback's<br />\ncorrectness even when it reads everything -- and <code>_TAIL_FULL_ASK_BOUND</code><br />\nitself is read from production, never a raised or re-declared literal<br />\nin this test.</p>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"event_loop_policy","time":{"start":1791980249757,"stop":1791980249757,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"tmp_path_factory","time":{"start":1791980249758,"stop":1791980249758,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"monkeypatch","time":{"start":1791980382204,"stop":1791980382204,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCoun